<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n91977" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῶμα</span></b>  (B), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πίνω,
		πέπωκα</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>drink,
			draught</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				266
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				715
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				392
			</span></i> (prob.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ba.</u>
				279
			</span></i> (prob.), <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				406a
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἀναγκαῖα π</span>.
				<i>drinking water</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				844b
			</span></i>: pl., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐτρεφέστατον
			πωμάτων</span>, of Dirce, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				308
			</span></i>(lyr.):—the short form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόμα</span></b>  occurs in <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				3.79
			</span></i> (metaph.), and in later Poets, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				8.20
			</span></i> P., <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Al.</u>
				105
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				299
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Man.
				3.71
			</span></i> (poet. dat. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πομάτεσσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hsch.
				</span></i>
			); also in Ionic and later Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>VM</u>
				5
			</span></i> (opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥύφημα</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Mus.</u>
				p.51
			</span></i> K., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				6.15
			</span></i>; but only as v.l. in correct Attic writers, as
				<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phd.</u>
				117b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Phlb.</u>
				34e
			</span></i>:—for <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πομάτιον</span></b>  in <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				578.8
			</span></i> Dind. restores <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόμα τι</span> from <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μελίτιον</span>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>drinking-cup</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
